

# The request in controlled English

The same requirement, said again in the controlled English the repository's reasoner reads, one sentence a line:

Mvccs is a program.
Mvccs simulates a tree.
Every tree is a b_tree.
The minimum_degree is 2.
Every b_tree holds the keys.
Every key is an integer.
Every negative_integer may be a key.
Every transaction has a snapshot.
Mvccs reads a line.
Every line holds a command.
Every line that is blank is ignored.
Every transaction begins at the latest_version.
Every repeated_begin begins an active_transaction.
Every repeated_begin causes an error.
Every transaction that is active may stage an insertion.
Every transaction that is active may stage a deletion.
Every transaction that is active may commit.
Every transaction that is active may abort.
Every transaction that is active may read a key.
Every transaction that is active may print the view.
Every transaction that is not active causes an error.
Every commit is atomic.
Every commit applies the changes to the latest_version.
Every commit creates a version.
Every commit increments the commit_id.
Every commit ends the transaction.
Every commit that is empty increments the commit_id.
Every abort discards the changes.
Every abort ends the transaction.
Every key that is visible reads as yes.
Every key that is not visible reads as no.
Every key that is visible is printed.
Every printing is ascending.
Every view that is empty does not print a line.
Every key that is committed gets yes.
Every key that is not committed gets no.
Every version_command prints the commit_id.
Every transaction_name is a word.
Every view is a snapshot.
Every view holds the staged changes.
Every commit that follows the snapshot is invisible.
Every key has a staged_change.
Every change that is last is kept.
Every blind_deletion deletes an invisible_key.
Every blind_deletion is staged.
Every committer that is last wins.
Every redundant_insertion inserts a present_key.
Every present_key is a committed_key.
Every redundant_insertion is ignored.
Every redundant_deletion deletes an absent_key.
Every absent_key is not a committed_key.
Every redundant_deletion is ignored.
Every unfinished_transaction is active.
Every unfinished_transaction is abandoned.
Every unfinished_transaction is not committed.
Every committed_version is a b_tree.
Every insertion is recursive.
Every deletion is recursive.
Every node is heap_allocated.
Every key_count is unbounded.
Every transaction_count is unbounded.
Every command prints an answer.
Mvccs does not print a prompt.
Mvccs does not print a debug_output.